id: pm-u2tqn6
title: "GH-776: preserve output override compatibility and export the public decision contract"
description: "The 2026.7.27 output_format override decision semantics can silently render the service context when legacy extensions return context.payload, while ServiceOverrideDecision is absent from public SDK authoring types."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T22:01:13.721Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:32:28.111Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:32:25.098Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: ServiceOverrideDecision is publicly exported from SDK and authoring surfaces; Legacy reference-identical payload pass-through declines safely with an actionable migration diagnostic; Extension fixtures and isolated package tests prove ordinary command output cannot be corrupted silently; SDK migration documentation explains handled and decline semantics
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make SDK extension override contracts explicit compatible and safe by default
value: Extension authors can customize rendering without silently corrupting every CLI response
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Hardened output service ownership compatibility and exported the typed public override decision contract.
expected_result: "SDK output service overrides remain backward compatible without silently owning output when returning the unchanged payload, and the decision type is publicly authorable."
actual_result: "Legacy echo returns now decline with a deprecation warning in synchronous and asynchronous hooks, and ServiceOverrideDecision is exported from the authoring surface."
